Read geom objects from an ASCII DXF file.

C = geom.read (FILE) returns what is in FILE: a
row cell array with one geom object per entity, in the order of the file,
nothing joined and nothing reclassified. LINE, ARC,
CIRCLE, LWPOLYLINE and a flat POLYLINE are
geom.Polyline objects; SPLINE and ELLIPSE are
geom.Spline objects, an ellipse as its exact rational spline; a
HATCH gives the geom.Region objects it fills. A
LINE slanting in three dimensions and a 3-D POLYLINE are
geom.Path objects, since no single plane holds them. Text,
dimensions, inserts, points, meshes and solids are skipped. An empty
file gives cell (1, 0).

A group the package wrote, through the write method of a
geom.Path or geom.Region or through geom.write, is
one element, the class its extended data names, so what was written is
what is read: a closed path stays a path, the route solid.sweep
turns into a ring, and a region keeps its holes.

Frames. Every geom object carries a geom.UCS, which the
package writes as extended data and reads back, for a flat object only
where the stored axes still lie in the entity's plane. A file without that
data is read in any plane: an entity whose normal is the z axis in
the world frame moved to its height, one whose normal points down the
z axis mirrored into the plane facing up first, as 2-D CAD programs
treat it, and any other in DXF's own frame for its plane. Paths and
splines are read in world coordinates.

C = geom.read (FILE, 'Layer', LAYER)
returns only what lies on the layer LAYER, its name compared without
regard to case, as CAD programs compare them.

G = geom.read (FILE, 'Type', TYPE)
builds the class TYPE names and returns one object of it:

'polyline'
A geom.Polyline, from one entity.
'spline'
A geom.Spline, from one entity.
'path'
A geom.Path, the entities chained end to end by
geom.Path.chain.
'region'
A geom.Region, the entities chained into closed loops and the loops
that share a plane nested by geom.Region.nest, an outline and its
holes.

The package's own groups count as built. Exactly one object must result.
More than one is an error naming the layer, as is finding objects on
several layers with no 'Layer' given, and finding none: separate
parts belong on separate layers, and 'Layer' picks one.

The width of a polyline is dropped, since a geom object has none.
Whatever is skipped, the widths dropped, and with 'Type' whatever
is left over, are reported in one warning, counted by entity type.

Coordinates are converted to millimetres from the units the file declares
in $INSUNITS; a file declaring none is read as millimetres. The
reader takes ASCII DXF from R12 (AC1009) to R2018
(AC1032). Text before R2007 is decoded from the code page the
header names, and from R2007 on as UTF-8. A binary DXF is an error.

R = geom.Region (geom.Polyline ([0, 0; 60, 0; 60, 40; 0, 40], ...
'Closed', true));
f = [tempname(), '.dxf'];
write (R, f);
B = geom.read (f, 'Type', 'region');
S = solid.extrude (B, 10);

