drafting: solid.Shape
A solid in millimetres, modelled through Open CASCADE.

solid.Shape holds the exact boundary of one or more solids: every
face a plane, cylinder, cone, sphere, torus or spline surface, every edge
a line, circle or curve, with nothing approximated by facets. It is what
the functions of the solid namespace create, what the boolean
operators combine, and what its write method saves as STEP for
exchange or STL for printing.

Primitives are made by

solid.box
solid.cylinder
solid.cone
solid.sphere
solid.ellipsoid
solid.torus
solid.wedge

and solids from +geom objects by

solid.extrude
solid.revolve
solid.loft
solid.sweep
solid.helix

A solid is made from a closed triangle mesh by solid.polyhedron,
and from a grid of points by solid.surface, which fits a surface
through the grid and thickens it. hull wraps shapes and points in
their convex hull, and solid.read loads solids from a STEP file.

Finally, shapes can be combined by the three boolean CAD operations, each
taking any number of shapes:

Method Result
union the material of any of them
subtract the material of the first that is in none of
the others
intersect the material common to all of them

Features are worked on a shape by methods: hole drills plain,
counterbored, countersunk and tapping holes, pocket cuts a region
into it, fillet and chamfer round or bevel edges, and
shell hollows the shape. The edges and faces they act on are
chosen by edges and faces, by the kind of curve or surface,
by direction and by position. section cuts a shape with a plane
into regions, which the solid functions build from again, and
projection gives the outline of a shape seen along a direction as
regions in the same way.

The class is a value class. Every operation returns a new shape
and leaves its operands unchanged, and a copy is independent of the
original. The empty shape adds nothing to a union and empties an
intersection, and a boolean whose result holds no material, such as the
intersection of two solids that do not meet, returns it. A shape is
saved and loaded with save and load like any other value.

See also:
solid.box,
solid.read,
solid.Shape.write,
solid.Shape.show


