# name: <cell-element>
# type: sq_string
# elements: 1
# length: 1006
drafting: S = solid.read (FILE)
Read a solid from a STEP file.

S = solid.read (FILE) returns the shapes held by the
STEP file FILE as one solid.Shape, in millimetres whatever
unit the file was written in. A file holding several parts returns them
together, and solid.Shape.numsolids counts them. The colour the
file gives a solid, or failing that the first of its faces with one, is
its row of solid.Shape.Colour.

STEP (ISO 10303-21) is the format every mechanical CAD program exchanges
solids in, and it keeps their exact geometry: a hole read from it is a true
cylinder, as it was modelled. A STEP file must end in .step, in
either case, and open with the keyword ISO-10303-21;, which may
follow white space and comments.

model.read reads the same file as a model.Assembly, its
parts named and placed as the file has them. A triangle mesh, from an
STL, OBJ or PLY file, is read by polymesh.read and made a solid by
solid.polyhedron.

See also:
